{"name":"Worsted Tan","hex":"#ab9379","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"worsted","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Yarn made from long strands of wool.","The fine, smooth fabric made from such wool yarn."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of worst"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worsted"},{"term":"tan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["The trigonometric function tangent."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Tangale."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tan"}],"entries":[{"title":"Worsted","blocks":[{"text":"Worsted is a high-quality type of wool yarn, the fabric made from this yarn, and a yarn weight category. The name derives from Worstead, a village in the English county of Norfolk. That village, together with North Walsham and Aylsham, formed a manufacturing centre for yarn and cloth in the 12th century, when pasture enclosure and liming rendered the East Anglian soil too rich for the older agrarian sheep breeds. In the same period, many weavers from the County of Flanders moved to Norfolk. \"Worsted\" yarns/fabrics are distinct from woollens : the former is considered stronger, finer, smoother, and harder than the latter."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Girl%27s_blue_worsted_wool_dress_-_DPLA_-_ae3977d739f9e65f7069b0410ffeb71f_%28page_1%29.jpg/330px-Girl%27s_blue_worsted_wool_dress_-_DPLA_-_ae3977d739f9e65f7069b0410ffeb71f_%28page_1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Worsted"},{"title":"Tan (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Tan is a pale tone of brown. The name is derived from tannum used in the tanning of leather."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Chestnut_Oak_Bark.jpg/330px-Chestnut_Oak_Bark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tan_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Hudson_Worsted_Company_mill%2C_March_2022.JPG/500px-Hudson_Worsted_Company_mill%2C_March_2022.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Hudson_Worsted_Company_mill%2C_March_2022.JPG/1280px-Hudson_Worsted_Company_mill%2C_March_2022.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Hudson_Worsted_Company_mill%2C_March_2022.JPG/500px-Hudson_Worsted_Company_mill%2C_March_2022.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A former worsted mill in Hudson, Massachusetts","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHudson_Worsted_Company_mill%2C_March_2022.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Tess_Designer_Yarns_Worsted_Merino.jpg/500px-Tess_Designer_Yarns_Worsted_Merino.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Tess_Designer_Yarns_Worsted_Merino.jpg/500px-Tess_Designer_Yarns_Worsted_Merino.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Worsted yarn made from Merino wool","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATess_Designer_Yarns_Worsted_Merino.jpg"}],"sounds":{"worsted":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b7/En-us-ncalif-worsted.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b7/En-us-ncalif-worsted.ogg/En-us-ncalif-worsted.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/70/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-worsted.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm